# .git is DELIBERATELY NOT excluded: Go's -buildvcs stamping reads it, and
# it is the only mechanism that puts a real revision into the image without
# a --build-arg path (docker/Dockerfile has a GIT_SHA fallback for a
# build-arg-driven pipeline, but the org-standard build path
# (actions/attest-build-provenance + a plain `docker build .`) does not
# pass one). Excluding .git is exactly the mistake that makes
# svc_build_info{revision=""} true in every image a real CI would produce
# while every gate keeps reporting the dimension delivered — see
# internal/platform/buildinfo/buildinfo_test.go's
# TestDockerignore_DoesNotExcludeGitWithoutAnLdflagsPath, which fails the
# build if this line is ever restored without also adding the ldflags path.
data
*.md
coverage.out
